<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02XJ">Corollary <span data-tag="02XJ">7.1.8.9</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category, let $B$ be a simplicial set, and let $f: K \rightarrow \operatorname{Fun}(B, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$ be a diagram. Assume that, for every vertex $b \in B$, the diagram </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[ K \xrightarrow {f} \operatorname{Fun}(B,\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \xrightarrow { \operatorname{ev}_ b } \operatorname{\mathcal{C}} \]
</div>
<p> has a colimit in $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. Then $f$ can be extended to a levelwise colimit diagram $\overline{f}: K^{\triangleright } \rightarrow \operatorname{Fun}(B,\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Apply Corollary <a data-tag="02XG" href="/tag/02XG">7.1.8.8</a> in the special case $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}= \Delta ^0$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
